# Working examples for the API. Load in VS Code (REST Client) or IntelliJ (HTTP Client).
# The backend runs on :8081 in dev; the SPA proxy also forwards /api there.
# Every response carries X-Request-Id (request tracing); errors carry it in the
# message as "(Reference: xxxx)" — grep the backend log for rid=xxxx.
@host = http://localhost:8081

### Legacy full-book policy list (SUPERVISOR only: every customer's number + holder
### name — claimants read their own rows via /mine, adjusters have no policy surface)
GET {{host}}/api/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health — public liveness probe for deploy orchestration (no auth, no DB check)
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Readiness — traffic gate: migrations current AND a query succeeds (public)
GET {{host}}/api/ready

### Claimant history — every claim this subject filed, newest first (CLAIMANT only)
# Public facts per row (status/product/loss date + decision when closed); never the
# reserve, notes, assignee, or coverage (the visibility wall holds per row).
GET {{host}}/api/claims/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Supervisor dashboard — aggregate ops numbers (SUPERVISOR only; 403 otherwise)
# Counts (open/unassigned/under-review/escalated/closed, 7-day aging pressure) plus the
# month-to-date approved indemnity total. Aggregates only, no per-claim data.
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### FNOL — file a claim (CLAIMANT only, 401 without a token)
# Flood guard: at most claims.fnol.rate-limit-per-day filings per claimant per rolling
# 24h (default 20) — beyond that the API answers 429 with a Retry-After hint.
# Validation: holder email must parse, loss date must be yyyy-MM-dd and not in the
# future, description <= 5000 chars, remarks <= 2000 chars.
# Auth: the SPA signs the user in via Keycloak (authorization-code + PKCE, public client
# "claims-frontend", realm "claims", http://localhost:8090). There is no password grant,
# so for ad-hoc requests grab an access token from a browser session on http://localhost:4200
# (DevTools -> Network -> any /api/claims request -> Authorization header) and paste it below.
# @token = <paste access token here>
POST {{host}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----ApiHttpBoundary

------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="policyNumber"\r
\r
POL-10001\r
------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="holderName"\r
\r
Ada Lovelace\r
------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="holderEmail"\r
\r
ada.lovelace@example.test\r
------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lossDate"\r
\r
2026-09-06\r
------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lossLocation"\r
\r
London\r
------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lossDescription"\r
\r
Kitchen flooded after a pipe burst.\r
------ApiHttpBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="covers"\r
\r
[{"coverCode":"HOSPITALIZATION","claimedAmount":200000},{"coverCode":"PHARMACY","claimedAmount":15000}]\r
# (photos are optional — add a part like the text ones above, name "photos", to upload)
------ApiHttpBoundary--\r

### FNOL — file a claim with a PDF attachment (CLAIMANT only, 401 without a token)
# Same shape as the FNOL example above, plus one "photos" part carrying a PDF
# (discharge summary / final bill). Create discharge-summary.pdf next to this file
# first — the server magic-byte gate needs real %PDF bytes; a renamed .exe/.txt is
# rejected with "Attachments must be image or PDF files." Stored rows pin sha256 +
# size_bytes; the attachment downloads via GET /api/claims/{n}/attachments/{id}.
POST {{host}}/api/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----ApiHttpPdfBoundary

------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="policyNumber"\r
\r
POL-10001\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="holderName"\r
\r
Ada Lovelace\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="holderEmail"\r
\r
ada.lovelace@example.test\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lossDate"\r
\r
2026-09-06\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lossLocation"\r
\r
London\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="lossDescription"\r
\r
Hospital stay after the accident; discharge summary attached.\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="covers"\r
\r
[{"coverCode":"HOSPITALIZATION","claimedAmount":200000}]\r
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="discharge-summary.pdf"\r
Content-Type: application/pdf\r
\r
< ./discharge-summary.pdf
------ApiHttpPdfBoundary--\r

### Adjuster queue — own claims (ADJUSTER_L1/L2) or the whole team (SUPERVISOR)
# Auth: access token from an adjuster/supervisor session (browser DevTools -> any
# /api/queue request -> Authorization header), pasted as {{token}} above.
GET {{host}}/api/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Claimant status — own claim only (CLAIMANT; someone else's claim is a 404)
# Response: claimant-view — claimNumber/status/steps, plus — only once the claim is CLOSED
# and decided — the decision: decision=APPROVED with the approved indemnityAmount, or
# decision=DENIED with the rationale as decisionRemarks. Undecided claims carry no decision
# fields at all; reserve/notes/assignee/coverage never appear (visibility wall holds on
# closed claims).
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Internal full view — policy + coverage + reserve + notes + photos
# (assigned adjuster or SUPERVISOR only; anyone else gets a 404)
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/full
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Set/update the reserve (assigned adjuster or SUPERVISOR)
PUT {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/reserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1500.00 }

### Set/update the reserve with optimistic concurrency (S5: send the loaded version)
# 409 shape on a stale version: {"error":"CONFLICT","message":"This claim changed
# since you opened it. Reload and retry."} — refetch the claim and retry with the new version.
PUT {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/reserve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1500.00, "expectedVersion": 0 }

### Add an internal note (assigned adjuster or SUPERVISOR)
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Coverage confirmed; awaiting builder quote." }

### Download a photo attachment (assigned adjuster or SUPERVISOR; served as an attachment)
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/attachments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Adjuster attach — upload a PDF to a claim (assigned adjuster or SUPERVISOR;
# anyone else gets a 404). Multipart `file` part + optional ?label. Use a real PDF
# (create final-bill.pdf next to this file) — spoofed bytes are rejected with
# "Attachments must be image or PDF files." Stored rows pin sha256 + size_bytes.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/attachments?label=Final%20bill
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----AttachPdfBoundary

------AttachPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="final-bill.pdf"\r
Content-Type: application/pdf\r
\r
< ./final-bill.pdf
------AttachPdfBoundary--\r

### Claimant NEED_INFO upload — upload a PDF to own claim in NEED_INFO
# (CLAIMANT; someone else's claim is a 404). Same multipart `file` shape as the
# adjuster attach above. Create discharge-summary.pdf next to this file first.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/documents?label=Discharge%20summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----ClaimantPdfBoundary

------ClaimantPdfBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="discharge-summary.pdf"\r
Content-Type: application/pdf\r
\r
< ./discharge-summary.pdf
------ClaimantPdfBoundary--\r

### Decide a claim (assigned ADJUSTER only — the authority gate)
# Approve within the actor's level limit -> records the single payment and closes the claim
# (rationale required). Above the actor's level -> never approved: the claim is escalated
# to L2 (response: escalatedTo=L2, status stays UNDER_REVIEW under the new L2 assignee) or
# to the supervisor (escalatedTo=SUPERVISOR, status ESCALATED_SUPERVISOR). DENIED always
# closes with the rationale as the claimant-visible remarks.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "APPROVED",
  "indemnityAmount": 1500.00,
  "rationale": "Quotes verified; within my authority."
}

### Decision: denial (closes the claim with remarks from the rationale)
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "DENIED",
  "rationale": "Coverage excludes the reported damage."
}

### Supervisor escalation queue — claims in ESCALATED_SUPERVISOR (SUPERVISOR only; 403 for
# adjusters/claimants). Auth: token from a supervisor session (DevTools -> Authorization).
GET {{host}}/api/escalations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Supervisor escalation decision — approve (record payment + close) or deny (close with
# remarks), on a claim in ESCALATED_SUPERVISOR. SUPERVISOR only; rationale required for
# both. An approval is not amount-gated (highest authority); the payment records a NULL
# authorizer (no supervisor app_user row) while the DECISION audit carries the subject.
# The decision email fires on closure, like the adjuster decision.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/escalation-decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "APPROVED",
  "indemnityAmount": 12000.00,
  "rationale": "Agreed under full authority."
}

### Escalation decision: denial (closes with the rationale as claimant-visible remarks)
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/escalation-decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "DENIED",
  "rationale": "The reported damage is outside the policy coverage."
}

### Staged workflow — full view (assignee or SUPERVISOR). Stage (REVIEW | VERIFICATION
# | DECISION), NEED_INFO state, per-cover money + outcomes + proposals, verification
# history, and the actor's authority limit + basis for this product. 404 otherwise.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/staged
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Staged workflow — review: advance REVIEW -> VERIFICATION (opens a PENDING
# verification row). Rationale required. Returns the staged view.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "ADVANCE",
  "rationale": "Documents look consistent; verifying the hospital stay."
}

### Staged workflow — review: reject at REVIEW (closes DENIED, rationale = remarks).
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "REJECT",
  "rationale": "The reported event is excluded by the policy clauses."
}

### Staged workflow — review: NEED_INFO (REVIEW or VERIFICATION only, never DECISION).
# Parks the claim (status NEED_INFO, assignee cleared, prior stage kept) until the
# claimant responds. Requested items required.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "NEED_INFO",
  "requestedItems": "Please upload the discharge summary and the final hospital bill."
}

### Staged workflow — open a verification (DIGITAL | PHYSICAL). Returns the row
# (status IN_PROGRESS, performedBy = caller).
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/verifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "DIGITAL",
  "notes": "Checking the hospital records against the claimed dates."
}

### Staged workflow — update a verification. COMPLETE requires outcome + notes;
# CANCELLED requires notes. Each write appends an audit row.
PUT {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/verifications/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "COMPLETE",
  "outcome": "PASSED",
  "notes": "Dates and amounts match the hospital records.",
  "evidenceRefs": "discharge-summary.pdf, final-bill.pdf"
}

### Staged workflow — assessment (VERIFICATION with a COMPLETE verification ->
# DECISION). Per-cover assessed amounts: 0 <= assessed <= claimed and within the
# cover sub-limit; assessed total within the remaining sum insured. Claim stays open
# on any violation (400 naming the remaining). Rationale required.
PUT {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/assessment
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "covers": [
    { "coverCode": "HOSPITALIZATION", "assessedAmount": 180000.00 },
    { "coverCode": "OPD", "assessedAmount": 25000.00 }
  ],
  "rationale": "Bills verified; room-rent cap applied."
}

### Staged workflow — cover decision (claims WITH covers). Per-cover APPROVED |
# REJECTED with approved/deductible/adjustment figures; net = max(approved -
# deductible + adjustment, 0). Pure rejection closes DENIED (never gated); within
# authority closes APPROVED (all approved) or PARTIALLY_APPROVED (mixed) with one
# payment = sum of nets; above authority saves proposals (is_proposal) and the claim
# STAYS open at DECISION for explicit referral — nothing moves by itself.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/cover-decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rationale": "Within my authority; deductibles per the policy schedule.",
  "covers": [
    { "coverCode": "HOSPITALIZATION", "decision": "APPROVED", "approvedAmount": 80000.00, "remarks": "Bills verified." },
    { "coverCode": "OPD", "decision": "REJECTED", "remarks": "OPD visits pre-date the policy waiting period." }
  ]
}

### Staged workflow — refer upwards (DECISION with saved proposals only). Named
# senior (higher rung whose limit covers the proposed total) or "auto": true (the
# least-loaded skilled adjuster at the lowest covering rung; supervisor fallback
# when no rung covers it). Stage preserved, proposals travel, caller loses access.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/refer
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "auto": true,
  "reason": "Proposed total is above my L1 authority; needs senior sign-off."
}

### Staged workflow — NEED_INFO response (CLAIMANT, own claim in NEED_INFO only).
# Returns the claim to its prior stage and reassigns it. Message optional.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/need-info-response
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Uploaded the discharge summary and the final bill."
}

### Staged workflow — supervisor cover-decision on an ESCALATED_SUPERVISOR claim
# (ungated, rationale required, atomic close + payment = sum of nets). Legacy
# no-cover claims keep the single-figure escalation-decision endpoint above.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/escalation-cover-decision
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rationale": "Senior review agrees with the proposed figures as revised.",
  "covers": [
    { "coverCode": "HOSPITALIZATION", "decision": "APPROVED", "approvedAmount": 80000.00 },
    { "coverCode": "OPD", "decision": "REJECTED", "remarks": "Outside the waiting period." }
  ]
}

### Authority config — list rows (SUPERVISOR only; 403 for adjusters/claimants). Each row:
# product code + route level (classifies new FNOL claims) + L1/L2 approval limits (the gate).
GET {{host}}/api/config/authority
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Authority config — edit one row (SUPERVISOR). The change feeds the next decision (gate)
# and the next filed claim (classification) immediately — no caching. Validation: route
# level L1/L2; amounts positive, <= 2 decimal places, L1 <= L2; unknown product -> 404.
PUT {{host}}/api/config/authority/HOME
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "routeLevel": "L1",
  "l1LimitAmount": 2500.00,
  "l2LimitAmount": 10000.00
}

### Reassign a claim to a target level (SUPERVISOR only) — routed to that level's
# least-loaded adjuster; the claim's level follows its new holder. Rejected for decided,
# supervisor-escalated, or invalid-level claims (400) and unknown claims (404). Audited as
# CLAIM_REASSIGNED with the supervisor as actor.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/reassign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "level": "L2"
}

### Claim audit log (SUPERVISOR only) — the claim's immutable history, oldest first.
# Append-only is enforced at the data layer (V7 trigger): raw UPDATE/DELETE are rejected.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Policy admin — create (SUPERVISOR only). Unknown product code -> 400 naming valid
# codes (10-row V2 catalog: HLTH-PLUS, AUTO-STD, PROP-HOME, ...); duplicate number
# -> 409. Coverage is a JSON object or omitted.
POST {{host}}/api/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-30001",
  "productCode": "HOME",
  "holderName": "Alice Example",
  "holderEmail": "alice@example.com",
  "coverage": {"type": "home", "sum_insured": 5000}
}

### Policy admin — CSV import (SUPERVISOR only). Multipart `file`, header
# policy_number,product_code,holder_name,holder_email,coverage (coverage optional raw
# JSON); <= 500 rows. Always HTTP 200 with the per-row summary
# [{row,policyNumber,ok,error}] — never a bare 500 on row 400; only a bad header or an
# over-limit file is a 400. Valid rows persist, bad rows report errors.
# Use a real file: create policies.csv with the header + rows, then uncomment:
# POST {{host}}/api/policies/import
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=import-boundary
#
# --import-boundary
# Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="policies.csv"
# Content-Type: text/csv
#
# < ./policies.csv
# --import-boundary--

### Policy admin — retire (SUPERVISOR only). ACTIVE -> RETIRED; already-RETIRED returns
# as-is. Unknown number -> 404. Retired policies stay readable for history; FNOL against
# one is rejected with the existing policy-mismatch 404 shape.
POST {{host}}/api/policies/POL-30001/retire
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Policy admin — list (SUPERVISOR only). All rows incl. RETIRED, newest first;
# page/size (defaults 0/25, max 100) + q (number/holder/product substring) + status
# (ACTIVE/RETIRED) filter. Envelope {content,page,size,totalElements,totalPages}.
GET {{host}}/api/policies/admin?page=0&size=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cockpit — my policies (CLAIMANT only). Policies whose holder_email matches the
# caller's token email, with remaining benefit per policy and per cover
# (remaining = sum_insured/sub-limit minus prior non-DENIED net payables; derived,
# never stored). Another holder's rows never leak; unlinked claimants get [].
GET {{host}}/api/policies/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cockpit — policy detail (owner only). One policy with its covers + remaining
# benefit. Non-owner (or unknown number) -> 404, never 403 (visibility wall).
GET {{host}}/api/policies/POL-10001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### FNOL filing covers — covers available for a holder-matched policy (CLAIMANT).
# Query: policyNumber + holderName + holderEmail (the typed filing identity, not the
# caller's account email). Holder mismatch or unknown policy -> 404, never 403.
# Returns [{coverCode, displayName, subLimit}]; 0/1 covers or 404 -> file legacy
# (omit the `covers` part). Selection is always optional; amounts must be > 0.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/filing-covers?policyNumber=POL-10001&holderName=Ada%20Lovelace&holderEmail=ada.lovelace@example.test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Email outbox — list (SUPERVISOR only). Rows newest first with status filter
# (PENDING/SENT/FAILED) + page/size + q (claim number/address/subject). Envelope
# {content,page,size,totalElements,totalPages}. Triage query for failures: filter
# status=FAILED — each row carries kind, claimNumber, attempts and last_error.
GET {{host}}/api/outbox?status=FAILED&page=0&size=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Email outbox — retry (SUPERVISOR only). Resets a FAILED row to PENDING (attempts
# preserved); retrying a SENT/PENDING row -> 400, unknown id -> 400.
POST {{host}}/api/outbox/1/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Required documents — list (staff: assignee or SUPERVISOR gets full rows)
# Full rows [{checkId, docKey, displayName, status, attachmentId, decidedBy,
# decidedAt}]; FNOL auto-seeds one PENDING row per required doc of the policy
# product (HEALTH: DISCHARGE_SUMMARY/FINAL_BILL/ID_PROOF; AUTO: PHOTOS/ESTIMATE/
# RC_COPY; PROPERTY: PHOTOS/ESTIMATE/OWNERSHIP_PROOF). Stranger -> 404, never 403.
# Find a checkId here for the link/waive examples below.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/required-documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Required documents — list (CLAIMANT: own claim, walled shape)
# Returns [{displayName, status}] only — no decided_by/attachmentId/checkId/audit
# internals (asserted by string-absence). Someone else's claim -> 404.
GET {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/required-documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Required documents — link an attachment (assignee or SUPERVISOR; 404 otherwise)
# The attachment must belong to the claim (else 404). Writes a DOC_LINKED audit
# row; the claimant tracker then shows the item RECEIVED. Find checkId/attachmentId
# via the staff GET above and the full view (attachments array).
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/required-documents/1/link
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attachmentId": 1
}

### Required documents — waive a check (assignee or SUPERVISOR; rationale required)
# Rationale missing/blank -> 400. Writes a DOC_WAIVED audit row with the rationale.
# Claimants get 403 on waive (strangers 404).
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/required-documents/1/waive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rationale": "ID already verified against the policy record."
}

### Adjuster attach — upload with docKey auto-link (assignee or SUPERVISOR)
# Optional `docKey` part (case-insensitive, e.g. FINAL_BILL) flips the matching
# PENDING check to RECEIVED (audited DOC_LINKED, first evidence wins). Unknown
# keys -> 400 naming the valid keys for the product. Create final-bill.pdf first.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/attachments?label=Final%20bill
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----AttachDocKeyBoundary

------AttachDocKeyBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="final-bill.pdf"\r
Content-Type: application/pdf\r
\r
< ./final-bill.pdf
------AttachDocKeyBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docKey"\r
\r
FINAL_BILL
------AttachDocKeyBoundary--\r

### Adjuster attach — upload v2 that supersedes v1 (assignee or SUPERVISOR)
# Optional advisory `docType` part (<=60 chars, else 400) + `replacesId` part
# (id of the prior attachment on the SAME claim; cross-claim or unknown id ->
# 404, never a leak). CLOSED claims still 400. The timeline entry for v2 gains
# " (supersedes: <v1 file name>)" text; AttachmentView carries docType +
# replacesId. docType is advisory — it does not drive the S3 docKey auto-link
# (pass both when the v2 is also the evidence for a required doc).
# Find v1's id via the full/staged view (attachments array).
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/attachments?label=Final%20bill%20(corrected)
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----AttachSupersedeBoundary

------AttachSupersedeBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="final-bill-v2.pdf"\r
Content-Type: application/pdf\r
\r
< ./final-bill-v2.pdf
------AttachSupersedeBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docType"\r
\r
FINAL_BILL
------AttachSupersedeBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="replacesId"\r
\r
1
------AttachSupersedeBoundary--\r

### Claimant documents — upload with docType (own claim in NEED_INFO; 404 otherwise)
# Same advisory `docType` part as the adjuster attach above (<=60 chars, else
# 400) + optional `replacesId` for a same-claim row. CLOSED claims still 400.
# Create corrected-bill.pdf next to this file first.
POST {{host}}/api/claims/CLM-000001/documents?label=Corrected%20bill
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----ClaimantDocTypeBoundary

------ClaimantDocTypeBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="corrected-bill.pdf"\r
Content-Type: application/pdf\r
\r
< ./corrected-bill.pdf
------ClaimantDocTypeBoundary\r
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="docType"\r
\r
FINAL_BILL
------ClaimantDocTypeBoundary--\r
